#!/bin/sh
# Prints the GitHub release notes for VERSION: its CHANGELOG.md section, then the text
# every release carries. Without a section, it warns and prints only the standard text.
set -eu

version=${1:?usage: scripts/release-notes VERSION}
root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)

section=$(awk -v heading="## $version" '
  $0 == heading { found = 1; next }
  found && /^## / { exit }
  found { print }
' "$root/CHANGELOG.md" | sed '/./,$!d')

if [ -n "$section" ]; then
  printf '%s\n\n---\n\n' "$section"
else
  echo "scripts/release-notes: CHANGELOG.md has no section for $version" >&2
fi
cat <<'TEXT'
DiskUse16x CLI archives for macOS and Linux in two free editions, Basic (diskuse16x-TARGET) and Pro (diskuse16x-pro-TARGET), .deb and .rpm packages of both editions for Linux, and the universal Mac app, with SHA-256 files and GitHub build-provenance attestations. Each CLI installs two commands, diskuse16x and its short name du16x. install.sh installs Basic, and install.sh --pro installs Pro. The engrmnaveed/tap Homebrew tap has the CLI formulas du16x and du16x-pro, and the diskuse16x cask for the Mac app. The Mac app is ad hoc signed and not notarized. Install it with Homebrew or download the ZIP. See docs/install.md for installation, verification, first-launch approval, and removal.
TEXT
